# dist/workstation/Caddyfile — the optional HTTPS front's config
# (polyforge#161, 84-image). Mounted read-only into the https-front
# service (docker compose --profile <boot> --profile https up -d).
#
# The site address is the operator's hostname (WORKSTATION_HTTPS_HOST,
# localhost by default): caddy serves ONLY the hostname the site
# address names and signs the internal-CA certificate for it, so a
# hardcoded service name would answer no request the browser makes.
# The same hostname must ride PI_WEB_ALLOWED_HOSTS — Pi Web trusts only
# loopback names, IP literals and the names that variable lists.
#
# The proxy target is the `workstation` network alias, which compose
# puts on BOTH boot services (the aihub variant carries no
# container_name of that name).
{$WORKSTATION_HTTPS_HOST:localhost} {
	tls internal
	reverse_proxy workstation:30141
}
